        <h2>Background</h2>
        <p>I am pursuing a B.S. in Computer Engineering at the University of California, San Diego. My coursework and projects have given me hands-on experience across embedded systems, digital logic, computer architecture, signal processing, machine learning, and web software.</p>
        <p>Outside the classroom, technical-support work taught me to diagnose real systems patiently: isolate the failure, test assumptions, communicate clearly, and leave the user with a reliable solution.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2>What I bring</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
            <li><strong>System thinking:</strong> sensors, firmware, communication, storage, interfaces, and enclosures.</li>
            <li><strong>Verification:</strong> unit tests, RTL testbenches, DRC/LVS, validation metrics, and reproducible experiments.</li>
            <li><strong>Hands-on work:</strong> circuit assembly, debugging, CAD, 3D printing, and computer repair.</li>
            <li><strong>Communication:</strong> fluent English and native Chinese.</li>
        </ul>
